{
  "v": 11,
  "label": "a fourth copy of one message into a collection takes the next free minted key, checked against every key the collection holds",
  "note": "Archive holds three copies of basic-1@example.org, all landed: the bare key under 1, the key minted over the provisional handle the bare key derives under 2, and that key minted again under 3. A fourth copy from INBOX is keyed by the identity minted over that provisional handle, minted again over each held key: the three are held, so it takes the fourth key, its own seq, and a pending create under the provisional handle that key derives. A key read against the bare key and its first mint alone would take the third's, which the write refuses, a binding pinning one handle, so the copy could never be staged (SYNC.md §7; STORAGE §9; live night 2026-11-23)",
